1
00:00:00,767 --> 00:00:03,760
<i>- Previously on</i> Gotham...
- I saw a vision

2
00:00:04,104 --> 00:00:05,538
<i>of a cataclysmic event.</i>

3
00:00:05,672 --> 00:00:06,696
(gunshot)

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,770
BRUCE: <i>We will create
a legacy in this city.</i>

5
00:00:09,276 --> 00:00:12,269
I think you could be so strong.

6
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:13,607
He sees it, too.

7
00:00:14,281 --> 00:00:16,250
BULLOCK: Jeremiah
escaped. He's got Bruce.

8
00:00:16,383 --> 00:00:18,409
JEROME: <i>I have bombs
planted around the city.</i>

9
00:00:18,552 --> 00:00:21,488
<i>I know seeing is believing,
and I do want you to believe me,</i>

10
00:00:21,622 --> 00:00:22,622
so...

11
00:00:24,558 --> 00:00:26,269
HARLAN: <i>Now, the governor's
declared the city off-limits</i>

12
00:00:26,293 --> 00:00:28,091
<i>until the situation
can be evaluated.</i>

13
00:00:28,228 --> 00:00:31,228
- In two hours, this city's
gonna be a battleground.
- Well, I'm not leaving.

14
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:33,865
RA'S AL GHUL: <i>Gotham is
soon to be each man for himself,</i>

15
00:00:34,201 --> 00:00:35,430
<i>a more savage place.</i>

16
00:00:35,569 --> 00:00:36,298
(grunts)

17
00:00:36,436 --> 00:00:39,634
What should I do with you?

18
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:42,268
OSWALD: You took
away the one person I love,

19
00:00:42,609 --> 00:00:44,771
so I took the one
person you love.

20
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:47,644
Out of this crucible of blood

21
00:00:47,781 --> 00:00:50,307
will rise the dark knight
that your city needs.

22
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:52,817
Gotham falls. We rise.

23
00:00:53,153 --> 00:00:55,088
(horns honking)

24
00:01:18,812 --> 00:01:20,405
(sirens wailing)

25
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:28,584
♪♪

26
00:01:32,159 --> 00:01:35,823
<i>- ♪ We'll meet again ♪</i>
- (gunshots)

27
00:01:36,496 --> 00:01:38,795
<i>♪ Don't know where ♪</i>

28
00:01:39,132 --> 00:01:42,193
<i>♪ Don't know when ♪</i>

29
00:01:42,336 --> 00:01:46,831
<i>♪ But I know we'll meet again ♪</i>

30
00:01:47,174 --> 00:01:53,205
<i>♪ Some sunny day. ♪</i>

31
00:01:54,681 --> 00:01:56,707
(record skips, music stops)

32
00:02:06,226 --> 00:02:08,218
(sirens wailing)

33
00:02:30,283 --> 00:02:32,275
♪♪

34
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:46,634
♪♪

35
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:13,494
♪♪

36
00:03:38,985 --> 00:03:40,715
Fire on my command!

37
00:03:40,854 --> 00:03:43,847
(guns clicking)

38
00:03:44,991 --> 00:03:46,254
For Gotham.

39
00:03:59,973 --> 00:04:01,942
♪♪

40
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,560
MAN (over radio):
<i>Listen, Gordon.</i>

41
00:04:08,648 --> 00:04:11,641
<i>Your people decided to
ignore evacuation orders...</i>

42
00:04:11,785 --> 00:04:12,862
GORDON: No, no, no, no, no.

43
00:04:12,886 --> 00:04:14,445
It is clear you
don't understand.

44
00:04:14,588 --> 00:04:16,420
MAN: <i>What's to
understand, Mr. Gordon?</i>

45
00:04:16,556 --> 00:04:18,252
<i>I'm afraid you are
not making your...</i>

46
00:04:18,391 --> 00:04:19,723
GORDON: For the last time,

47
00:04:20,627 --> 00:04:22,391
after the bridges blew
and the government

48
00:04:22,529 --> 00:04:24,395
declared Gotham off-limits,

49
00:04:24,831 --> 00:04:26,629
the city was up for grabs.

50
00:04:27,634 --> 00:04:29,865
Given over to
criminals and murderers.

51
00:04:30,904 --> 00:04:32,839
Now, territory is
controlled by whoever has

52
00:04:32,973 --> 00:04:34,805
enough power to hold it.

53
00:04:35,542 --> 00:04:38,478
(scoffs) I mean, we have Penguin
in City Hall, for God's sakes.

54
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:43,015
<i>He raided the armory
and stockpiled weapons,</i>

55
00:04:43,416 --> 00:04:46,386
<i>then repurposed a factory
to manufacture ammunition.</i>

56
00:04:52,058 --> 00:04:53,058
(gunshot)

57
00:04:58,799 --> 00:05:00,563
<i>It's made him unassailable.</i>

58
00:05:01,768 --> 00:05:05,000
<i>Barbara and the Sirens
control an area around their club.</i>

59
00:05:05,338 --> 00:05:07,830
<i>It's the only place in
Gotham not suffering for food,</i>

60
00:05:08,041 --> 00:05:09,041
<i>or booze.</i>

61
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:12,008
<i>Barbara trades
mainly in information.</i>

62
00:05:12,913 --> 00:05:14,711
Just be gone by midnight.

63
00:05:15,615 --> 00:05:19,347
<i>It's women only, but men
can buy windows of time.</i>

64
00:05:21,521 --> 00:05:24,013
It's two minutes past
pumpkin time, sweetheart.

65
00:05:24,357 --> 00:05:25,552
- Wait.
- GORDON: <i>Word is...</i>

66
00:05:26,393 --> 00:05:26,917
(grunting)

67
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:29,325
<i>she enforces her
rule with an iron hand.</i>

68
00:05:30,497 --> 00:05:33,433
To the west is Jonathan Crane,

69
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:35,501
the Scarecrow.

70
00:05:35,535 --> 00:05:37,561
(grunting and groaning)

71
00:05:37,704 --> 00:05:38,704
(growls)

72
00:05:38,738 --> 00:05:40,866
(man whimpering,
pleading indistinctly)

73
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,976
(all cheering)

74
00:05:46,112 --> 00:05:48,707
(screaming)

75
00:05:49,082 --> 00:05:52,883
Victor Fries is further north
and warring with Firefly.

76
00:05:53,486 --> 00:05:55,978
And to date, there have
been no confirmed sightings

77
00:05:56,122 --> 00:05:57,750
of Jeremiah Valeska.

78
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:02,488
Then there's us.

79
00:06:03,496 --> 00:06:06,989
GCPD controls a ten-block
area around the precinct,

80
00:06:07,133 --> 00:06:10,399
<i>where we feed and
protect 150 civilians.</i>

81
00:06:10,871 --> 00:06:12,871
<i>That number could grow as
who knows how many others</i>

82
00:06:12,973 --> 00:06:14,703
<i>are trapped around the city.</i>

83
00:06:15,041 --> 00:06:16,452
<i>These are people
who couldn't get out</i>

84
00:06:16,476 --> 00:06:17,808
<i>when the city was abandoned.</i>

85
00:06:17,944 --> 00:06:20,072
<i>The poor, the
sick, whole families.</i>

86
00:06:20,413 --> 00:06:21,745
<i>The government has a duty.</i>

87
00:06:22,549 --> 00:06:24,780
You have a duty to help them.

88
00:06:24,918 --> 00:06:25,942
MAN: <i>Mr. Gordon...</i>

89
00:06:26,419 --> 00:06:27,614
Captain Gordon.

90
00:06:27,754 --> 00:06:30,087
MAN: <i>We've been over
this time and time again.</i>

91
00:06:30,423 --> 00:06:32,619
<i>No one is allowed
in or out of Gotham.</i>

92
00:06:32,826 --> 00:06:34,590
People we are protecting
are not criminals.

93
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:36,808
MAN: <i>And anyone who
stayed after the evacuation order</i>

94
00:06:36,930 --> 00:06:38,922
<i>is no longer the
government's responsibility.</i>

95
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:40,931
We are surrounded
by hostile forces.

96
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,968
We are running out
of food, ammunition.

97
00:06:43,103 --> 00:06:45,436
There are children here.
You have to evacuate them.

98
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:47,139
MAN: <i>A committee is being formed</i>

99
00:06:47,474 --> 00:06:49,670
<i>regarding the
situation in Gotham.</i>

100
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:50,910
(quietly): Committee.

101
00:06:53,013 --> 00:06:55,573
At least let us
resupply ourselves.

102
00:06:56,049 --> 00:06:58,143
MAN: <i>We understand
the situation.</i>

103
00:06:58,485 --> 00:06:59,485
You don't understand.

104
00:06:59,619 --> 00:07:00,830
If you did, you
would do something.

105
00:07:00,854 --> 00:07:02,083
Just say we're on our own.

106
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:04,891
(radio static warbling
and crackling)

107
00:07:19,072 --> 00:07:21,098
DOCTOR: Paralysis
aside, we need to operate

108
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,842
before her spine
collapses upon itself.

109
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,840
In truth, she should
have been evacuated.

110
00:07:26,746 --> 00:07:27,857
ALFRED: Yeah, well,
we tried to get her out

111
00:07:27,881 --> 00:07:29,577
the night that
everything went to hell.

112
00:07:30,216 --> 00:07:31,878
And then they blew
the bloody bridges.

113
00:07:33,586 --> 00:07:34,849
BRUCE: Can you operate here?

114
00:07:36,222 --> 00:07:38,020
I don't think we have a choice.

115
00:07:44,597 --> 00:07:45,597
Selina?

116
00:07:46,833 --> 00:07:48,461
(shuddering breaths)

117
00:07:48,601 --> 00:07:49,728
The doctor wants to operate.

118
00:07:49,869 --> 00:07:50,869
Fine.

119
00:07:54,741 --> 00:07:55,800
Whatever.

120
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,987
I'm gonna be here
the whole time.

121
00:08:17,097 --> 00:08:18,258
(angry shouting)

122
00:08:18,665 --> 00:08:19,189
Enough!

123
00:08:19,532 --> 00:08:20,556
You cops are getting fat

124
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,020
while the rest of
us are starving!

125
00:08:22,102 --> 00:08:23,195
That's right.

126
00:08:23,536 --> 00:08:24,936
While the rest of
us are starving!

127
00:08:25,071 --> 00:08:26,751
- You hungry? Yeah?
- (clamoring continues)

128
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,751
- The cops get more!
- I got something
you can chew on.

129
00:08:28,775 --> 00:08:29,936
Harvey, Harvey! May I? May I?

130
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:32,138
Everyone. Sir?

131
00:08:32,278 --> 00:08:35,544
- Everyone gets the same share,
police and civilians alike.
- (others jeering)

132
00:08:35,682 --> 00:08:38,777
If we start handing out
more, the supplies will not last.

133
00:08:38,918 --> 00:08:41,649
You're lying. He's lying!

134
00:08:41,788 --> 00:08:42,788
The cops get more.

135
00:08:42,822 --> 00:08:44,518
- You shut up!
- GORDON:
That's enough!

136
00:08:44,657 --> 00:08:46,751
(clamoring quiets)

137
00:08:50,964 --> 00:08:53,092
You don't like the rules, leave.

138
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:55,964
I'm just saying...

139
00:08:56,102 --> 00:08:58,628
Say it walking, putz.

140
00:08:59,606 --> 00:09:00,606
(scattered shouts)

141
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:01,707
MEN: Come on!

142
00:09:01,741 --> 00:09:02,741
MAN: You look well fed!

143
00:09:02,876 --> 00:09:03,876
Let's go.

144
00:09:05,812 --> 00:09:06,822
OFFICER: Hey,
come on, listen up.

145
00:09:06,846 --> 00:09:07,677
Move it out of here.

146
00:09:07,814 --> 00:09:08,814
Move it.

147
00:09:09,649 --> 00:09:11,277
(door closes)

148
00:09:12,952 --> 00:09:15,148
GORDON: So, how we doing?

149
00:09:15,288 --> 00:09:17,052
LUCIUS: Well, we
got a month of food left.

150
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:19,056
Less if refugees keep coming.

151
00:09:20,026 --> 00:09:22,086
What'd the Department
of Douchebaggery say?

152
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:23,228
GORDON: <i>Same as always.</i>

153
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:24,563
Not sending any help.

154
00:09:24,864 --> 00:09:25,864
Not letting anyone leave.

155
00:09:25,965 --> 00:09:27,243
- I had to try.
- I swear to God,

156
00:09:27,267 --> 00:09:29,236
I am never paying taxes again.

157
00:09:29,669 --> 00:09:30,830
And if people ask?

158
00:09:32,105 --> 00:09:33,105
Tell 'em sooner or later,

159
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:34,901
the government
will do the right thing.

160
00:09:35,708 --> 00:09:37,268
Rebuild the bridges,
take back the city.

161
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:38,738
Just have to be patient.

162
00:09:38,878 --> 00:09:41,143
And the truth? We're on our own.

163
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:44,217
The truth is we have no
idea what might happen.

164
00:09:44,751 --> 00:09:47,152
And our job is to
keep ourselves...

165
00:09:48,121 --> 00:09:49,783
and everyone else alive.

166
00:09:50,023 --> 00:09:52,268
BULLOCK: <i>We're down to our
last rounds of ammo. What if...</i>

167
00:09:52,292 --> 00:09:54,284
Penguin or someone else
decides to make a move?

168
00:09:54,627 --> 00:09:56,152
We're sitting ducks here, man.

169
00:09:56,296 --> 00:09:59,664
♪♪

170
00:10:01,868 --> 00:10:03,803
(birds squawking,
buoy bell clanging)

171
00:10:06,372 --> 00:10:08,000
(snores, moans)

172
00:10:08,141 --> 00:10:10,337
(wings fluttering,
pigeons cooing)

173
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:12,977
(gasps, grunts)

174
00:10:13,113 --> 00:10:14,979
(sofa creaking)

175
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:18,779
(siren whooping, engine revving)

176
00:10:18,918 --> 00:10:21,353
♪♪

177
00:10:21,688 --> 00:10:22,815
(gasps)

178
00:10:24,724 --> 00:10:25,316
(sighs)

179
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:27,025
- (dog growling)
- (gasps)

180
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,026
(barking)

181
00:10:31,731 --> 00:10:33,723
♪♪

182
00:10:43,776 --> 00:10:44,776
NYGMA: <i>Okay.</i>

183
00:10:45,011 --> 00:10:46,343
Where was I?

184
00:10:46,846 --> 00:10:47,939
Happened again.

185
00:10:48,281 --> 00:10:50,079
This time, woke up on a rooftop.

186
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,879
Same thing.

187
00:10:53,286 --> 00:10:54,286
No idea how I got there

188
00:10:54,354 --> 00:10:56,074
or what happened during
the preceding hours.

189
00:11:03,730 --> 00:11:05,130
Show yourself.

190
00:11:06,399 --> 00:11:08,834
I know it's you
inside there, Ed.

191
00:11:12,772 --> 00:11:14,138
Show yourself.

192
00:11:17,310 --> 00:11:19,802
Idiot Ed still won't appear.

193
00:11:20,847 --> 00:11:21,906
Coward.

194
00:11:22,982 --> 00:11:25,062
But I know it's him controlling
me when I'm sleeping.

195
00:11:29,255 --> 00:11:30,255
Why?

196
00:11:31,791 --> 00:11:33,419
What is he doing?

197
00:11:44,003 --> 00:11:46,472
You know, you could get
someone else to turn on the spotlight.

198
00:11:49,075 --> 00:11:50,839
I like doing it.

199
00:11:51,911 --> 00:11:53,722
Because it reminds people
that even in darkness,

200
00:11:53,746 --> 00:11:54,746
there is light.

201
00:11:55,882 --> 00:11:57,282
And it reminds me.

202
00:11:59,886 --> 00:12:01,445
We're low on supplies.

203
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:05,187
Government won't
evac, won't send in help.

204
00:12:06,826 --> 00:12:08,226
It doesn't make sense.

205
00:12:10,797 --> 00:12:12,037
I imagine, from where they sit,

206
00:12:12,131 --> 00:12:14,464
it's pretty easy to
ignore people's suffering.

207
00:12:19,005 --> 00:12:21,450
I gave Lucius permission to raid
the Wayne Enterprises R & D lab

208
00:12:21,474 --> 00:12:23,136
for whatever he could scavenge.

209
00:12:23,810 --> 00:12:25,721
He's working on night
vision goggles for your men.

210
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,441
- It's not much.
- Everything helps.

211
00:12:30,183 --> 00:12:32,982
Bruce, we stayed because people
here still here need protection.

212
00:12:33,119 --> 00:12:34,451
That hasn't changed.

213
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:41,894
I should go.

214
00:12:43,363 --> 00:12:46,197
The doctor's worried Selina's
condition is getting worse.

215
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:48,532
They're going to operate.

216
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:52,132
Let me know how it goes.

217
00:12:59,212 --> 00:13:00,840
Are you sorry you stayed?

218
00:13:04,250 --> 00:13:05,250
No.

219
00:13:06,185 --> 00:13:07,185
You?

220
00:13:09,188 --> 00:13:10,212
Hell no.

221
00:13:31,511 --> 00:13:34,037
MR. PENN: Mr. Cobblepot
offers a thousand rounds

222
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:36,979
of freshly minted
nine-millimeter stock

223
00:13:37,317 --> 00:13:38,546
for a thousand pounds

224
00:13:38,885 --> 00:13:40,080
of grade-A steak.

225
00:13:40,219 --> 00:13:43,018
Hmm, so what
we're hearing is true.

226
00:13:43,523 --> 00:13:45,549
Cupboard's a bit
bare in Penguinland?

227
00:13:46,893 --> 00:13:48,191
Absolutely not.

228
00:13:49,062 --> 00:13:51,327
Mr. Cobblepot just had
a hankering for red meat.

229
00:13:51,464 --> 00:13:54,229
Ugh, please. Ozzie
wants to get fat on rib eye

230
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,892
while his minions
starve. Shocker.

231
00:13:57,070 --> 00:13:58,265
TABITHA: I have a question.

232
00:13:58,905 --> 00:14:01,932
Why hasn't your boss left his
citadel since the bridges blew?

233
00:14:02,942 --> 00:14:04,934
He scared I'm gonna
stick him in the throat?

234
00:14:05,078 --> 00:14:06,798
BARBARA: Tabby's still
raw from when Penguin

235
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:08,223
murdered Butch
right in front of her,

236
00:14:08,247 --> 00:14:11,081
so it'll have to
be 2,000 rounds.

237
00:14:11,217 --> 00:14:13,152
Barbara, we're not giving
that bastard anything.

238
00:14:13,886 --> 00:14:17,084
Exactly. We're trading
for something we need.

239
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:18,449
No.

240
00:14:20,326 --> 00:14:23,160
Honey, no one is asking you

241
00:14:23,296 --> 00:14:24,889
to forget what happened,

242
00:14:25,231 --> 00:14:27,962
but how do we protect the
women who come in here every day

243
00:14:28,101 --> 00:14:29,364
looking for safety?

244
00:14:30,036 --> 00:14:31,334
We need this.

245
00:14:32,438 --> 00:14:34,134
Penguin's time will come.

246
00:14:34,474 --> 00:14:35,533
I promise.

247
00:14:37,577 --> 00:14:38,636
(scoffs)

248
00:14:48,921 --> 00:14:51,254
He's gonna regret
giving me this.

249
00:14:55,161 --> 00:14:57,153
Better make it 3,000 rounds.

250
00:15:01,234 --> 00:15:03,362
(indistinct radio chatter)

251
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:07,266
OFFICER: Something's out there.

252
00:15:08,408 --> 00:15:12,311
- There. See? The shadow moved.
- (second officer laughs)

253
00:15:12,445 --> 00:15:14,471
It's just a shadow, man.

254
00:15:14,614 --> 00:15:17,311
No. Something's out there.

255
00:15:22,221 --> 00:15:23,985
There. See?

256
00:15:25,691 --> 00:15:26,691
(growls)

257
00:15:27,026 --> 00:15:29,518
(screaming)

258
00:15:29,695 --> 00:15:30,695
Hey, you okay?

259
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:32,564
(screaming continues)

260
00:15:32,698 --> 00:15:33,698
You okay?

261
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,235
Would you like
me to make it stop?

262
00:15:37,036 --> 00:15:38,629
(whimpering): Yes.

263
00:15:39,038 --> 00:15:40,336
Open this door.

264
00:15:40,506 --> 00:15:42,099
(grunting)

265
00:15:42,241 --> 00:15:43,607
No, no, no! Don't open the gate!

266
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:46,469
(alarm buzzing)

267
00:15:46,979 --> 00:15:48,413
(groaning)

268
00:15:50,516 --> 00:15:53,281
Split up. Take what we came for.

269
00:15:54,487 --> 00:15:57,184
Kill whoever stands in your way.

270
00:15:57,623 --> 00:16:01,060
Show these fools
the face of fear.

271
00:16:01,194 --> 00:16:02,719
(others shouting)

272
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:04,628
These here are the weak points.

273
00:16:05,231 --> 00:16:07,723
Reinforce all barriers that
front Penguin's territory.

274
00:16:08,067 --> 00:16:09,126
I want to be ready.

275
00:16:09,502 --> 00:16:11,471
(electrical buzzing
and whirring)

276
00:16:16,476 --> 00:16:17,535
HARPER: What the hell?

277
00:16:18,110 --> 00:16:19,578
(quiet, indistinct chatter)

278
00:16:25,084 --> 00:16:26,108
Find Lucius.

279
00:16:26,385 --> 00:16:28,183
Tell him to meet
me at the generator.

280
00:16:31,023 --> 00:16:33,117
(machine beeping)

281
00:16:49,609 --> 00:16:51,043
Lights are out everywhere.

282
00:16:51,310 --> 00:16:52,588
Well, don't you
worry, Master Bruce.

283
00:16:52,612 --> 00:16:54,342
Clinic's got its own
backup generator.

284
00:16:54,514 --> 00:16:57,712
(clanking, electrical buzzing)

285
00:16:58,551 --> 00:16:59,280
You see?

286
00:16:59,385 --> 00:17:01,411
Everything's shipshape
and Bristol fashion.

287
00:17:01,721 --> 00:17:02,721
No.

288
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:05,023
Something's wrong.

289
00:17:05,658 --> 00:17:07,593
Men in the basement.

290
00:17:08,127 --> 00:17:09,447
They're stealing
all the medicine.

291
00:17:10,663 --> 00:17:11,687
Alfred, stay with Selina.

292
00:17:12,431 --> 00:17:13,742
Of course, but you
can't go down there.

293
00:17:13,766 --> 00:17:16,167
It's gonna be pitch black.
Gonna need a torch or something.

294
00:17:16,636 --> 00:17:18,264
Lucius gave me something better.

295
00:17:21,474 --> 00:17:23,102
- Careful.
- (door closes)

296
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:26,175
(door creaking)

297
00:17:29,749 --> 00:17:30,749
(door closes)

298
00:17:31,384 --> 00:17:33,819
(buzzing, crackling)

299
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:55,833
(metallic scraping
and clanging; grunting)

300
00:17:56,542 --> 00:17:58,534
I know what you're
thinking, Captain.

301
00:17:59,645 --> 00:18:01,307
I have so few bullets.

302
00:18:01,814 --> 00:18:03,715
Do I spend one on him?

303
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:05,411
Is it worth it?

304
00:18:06,786 --> 00:18:08,516
I already know it's not.

305
00:18:10,222 --> 00:18:11,417
My other question is:

306
00:18:11,557 --> 00:18:13,788
Why are you here? It's
not to steal the generator.

307
00:18:14,193 --> 00:18:16,185
Why would I want light?

308
00:18:16,362 --> 00:18:18,763
Fear lives in darkness.

309
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:21,791
So what then? You
came for our supplies?

310
00:18:22,134 --> 00:18:23,158
Exactly so.

311
00:18:23,336 --> 00:18:26,135
But since I'm here,
I'll also take your life.

312
00:18:26,305 --> 00:18:29,503
(grunting)

313
00:18:38,584 --> 00:18:41,713
It's been a while since you
tasted my toxin, Captain.

314
00:18:42,288 --> 00:18:43,779
What are you scared of now?

315
00:18:44,657 --> 00:18:45,657
Not you.

316
00:18:48,661 --> 00:18:50,493
(screaming)

317
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:55,329
(explosive whoosh)

318
00:18:59,205 --> 00:19:00,205
(frantic chatter)

319
00:19:00,239 --> 00:19:01,639
Hey! Hey!

320
00:19:01,774 --> 00:19:04,710
- (gunfire, bullets ricocheting)
- Hey!

321
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:09,473
They got the beans.

322
00:19:10,282 --> 00:19:12,513
(quiet, indistinct chatter)

323
00:19:13,185 --> 00:19:14,265
Go. The lights are back up.

324
00:19:14,353 --> 00:19:15,412
Go! Move! Go!

325
00:19:15,554 --> 00:19:17,523
(high-pitched whirring)

326
00:19:19,458 --> 00:19:21,791
(gasps) Did...
did you hear that?

327
00:19:22,895 --> 00:19:24,420
(yells)

328
00:19:36,742 --> 00:19:38,301
(grunting)

329
00:19:39,779 --> 00:19:40,803
Hello?

330
00:19:42,915 --> 00:19:44,213
Scag?

331
00:19:44,784 --> 00:19:46,309
Hey... hey, guys?

332
00:19:47,286 --> 00:19:48,345
Scag?

333
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:53,524
Hey, guys, this
isn't... this isn't funny.

334
00:19:58,564 --> 00:20:00,226
(grunting)

335
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:01,710
- (high-pitched ringing)
- (screams)

336
00:20:01,734 --> 00:20:03,794
(grunting, gasping)

337
00:20:03,936 --> 00:20:05,700
Go back! Go back!

338
00:20:05,838 --> 00:20:07,636
(panting, frantic chatter)

339
00:20:15,414 --> 00:20:17,440
(tires squealing,
sirens wailing)

340
00:20:17,583 --> 00:20:18,812
(clamoring)

341
00:20:18,951 --> 00:20:20,852
First their government
abandons them,

342
00:20:21,353 --> 00:20:23,073
and then some freak
dressed like a scarecrow

343
00:20:23,289 --> 00:20:24,382
steals their grub.

344
00:20:24,590 --> 00:20:25,853
I'd be pissed, too.

345
00:20:26,625 --> 00:20:27,625
So where are we?

346
00:20:28,294 --> 00:20:29,387
At current consumption,

347
00:20:29,528 --> 00:20:30,996
we've got a week of food.

348
00:20:31,597 --> 00:20:32,656
Go to half rations.

349
00:20:32,798 --> 00:20:34,391
We're already at half rations.

350
00:20:34,934 --> 00:20:36,266
Cut 'em again.

351
00:20:36,402 --> 00:20:37,631
The people won't be happy.

352
00:20:37,770 --> 00:20:39,398
I haven't been
happy in ten years.

353
00:20:39,605 --> 00:20:40,834
At least they'll be alive.

354
00:20:40,973 --> 00:20:43,442
All right, that buys us
two weeks. Then what?

355
00:20:43,943 --> 00:20:44,706
Jim, at this point,

356
00:20:44,844 --> 00:20:46,555
the bastards across the
river are gonna have to

357
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:48,411
- step up and help.
- Why start now?

358
00:20:48,547 --> 00:20:49,547
They haven't before.

359
00:20:49,582 --> 00:20:51,448
For the love of God,
we... because we stayed

360
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:52,950
to do the job they wouldn't.

361
00:20:53,385 --> 00:20:55,377
Huh? And now they're just
gonna sit back and watch

362
00:20:55,521 --> 00:20:57,319
while we starve or
tear ourselves apart?

363
00:20:57,456 --> 00:20:58,500
Because that's
what's gonna happen.

364
00:20:58,524 --> 00:20:59,548
I know, Harv.

365
00:20:59,692 --> 00:21:01,812
But right now, we have to
tell these people something.

366
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:03,452
BRUCE: Tell them help is coming.

367
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:06,626
I'll fly in supplies.

368
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:09,324
We tried that.

369
00:21:09,468 --> 00:21:11,266
We couldn't even get
permission to take off.

370
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:12,836
Zero tolerance.
Nothing in or out.

371
00:21:13,005 --> 00:21:14,685
BRUCE: Well, I'm not
asking for permission.

372
00:21:15,708 --> 00:21:16,708
It's ready.

373
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:18,420
Alfred's already radioed
to have it delivered

374
00:21:18,444 --> 00:21:19,537
from our east bay hangar.

375
00:21:19,979 --> 00:21:21,845
We can have a supply
chopper here within hours.

376
00:21:23,949 --> 00:21:26,748
Man, it is nice to have
a billionaire around.

377
00:21:26,919 --> 00:21:27,919
Even if it succeeds,

378
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:29,319
the government's gonna find out.

379
00:21:29,455 --> 00:21:30,684
It's a one-time solution.

380
00:21:31,023 --> 00:21:33,049
Scarecrow's men
didn't just take food.

381
00:21:35,494 --> 00:21:37,360
They stole medicine
from the clinic.

382
00:21:40,032 --> 00:21:41,728
There are people in pain.

383
00:21:47,006 --> 00:21:49,066
Harvey, tell the people
help is on the way.

384
00:21:49,575 --> 00:21:50,575
You got it.

385
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:55,780
How's Selina?

386
00:21:59,718 --> 00:22:01,016
She's strong.

387
00:22:02,488 --> 00:22:03,854
She'll pull through.

388
00:22:16,468 --> 00:22:18,937
Doc says the surgery
was a success.

389
00:22:20,573 --> 00:22:22,906
My spine's not
gonna turn to jelly.

390
00:22:24,777 --> 00:22:26,837
Still never be able
to walk again, so...

391
00:22:27,379 --> 00:22:28,677
that's a bummer.

392
00:22:31,417 --> 00:22:33,386
There's limited resources here.

393
00:22:34,453 --> 00:22:36,718
But there's hope once
we join the mainland.

394
00:22:37,790 --> 00:22:38,790
Gee.

395
00:22:40,059 --> 00:22:42,119
For a second
there, I was worried.

396
00:22:43,796 --> 00:22:45,924
Selina, I know you're in pain.

397
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:49,466
Some medicine is on its way.

398
00:22:50,569 --> 00:22:52,060
You know what's funny?

399
00:22:55,140 --> 00:22:57,632
Jeremiah shot me to get to you.

400
00:23:02,081 --> 00:23:04,107
After all the
things I've done...

401
00:23:07,119 --> 00:23:09,554
what did me in was
being your friend.

402
00:23:15,527 --> 00:23:17,689
I just wish Jeremiah killed me.

403
00:23:36,415 --> 00:23:37,713
Doctors can't help her.

404
00:23:41,420 --> 00:23:43,889
She needs the witch.

405
00:23:48,127 --> 00:23:49,823
(indistinct chatter)

406
00:23:49,995 --> 00:23:51,088
MAN: Thank you.

407
00:23:52,631 --> 00:23:53,792
How's the mood?

408
00:23:53,933 --> 00:23:55,162
They're hanging in there.

409
00:23:56,669 --> 00:23:58,194
They love their Jim Gordon.

410
00:23:58,871 --> 00:24:02,069
But if that chopper
doesn't come, it'll be bad.

411
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:09,007
It'll come.

412
00:24:10,716 --> 00:24:12,685
(operatic music playing)

413
00:24:14,086 --> 00:24:15,086
(groans)

414
00:24:22,094 --> 00:24:23,221
Feels good.

415
00:24:25,064 --> 00:24:26,760
Missing something, though.

416
00:24:28,968 --> 00:24:30,664
Put a knife on it.

417
00:24:32,805 --> 00:24:34,797
- (laughing)
- (door opens)

418
00:24:34,940 --> 00:24:37,535
Another shutdown at the factory.

419
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:41,209
A worker fell into
a hydraulic press.

420
00:24:41,547 --> 00:24:43,778
It appears he passed
out from hunger.

421
00:24:44,183 --> 00:24:47,051
Sir, I worry if we don't
increase the food allowance...

422
00:24:47,186 --> 00:24:47,983
Mr. Penn,

423
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:50,954
I feel for all of our workers.

424
00:24:51,523 --> 00:24:54,550
But I cannot give
what I do not have.

425
00:25:00,833 --> 00:25:02,563
Overcooked!

426
00:25:02,868 --> 00:25:04,063
(dog pants, whines)

427
00:25:04,203 --> 00:25:05,203
(sighs)

428
00:25:06,672 --> 00:25:07,503
Edward.

429
00:25:07,639 --> 00:25:09,130
(laughs)

430
00:25:11,844 --> 00:25:14,279
Such a good boy.

431
00:25:14,613 --> 00:25:16,241
(laughing)

432
00:25:17,649 --> 00:25:20,141
Quality at the factory
is also suffering.

433
00:25:20,652 --> 00:25:22,848
- More misfires...
- Nonsense.

434
00:25:22,988 --> 00:25:24,149
- (gunshot)
- (whimpers)

435
00:25:25,090 --> 00:25:26,558
Our rounds are fine.

436
00:25:26,925 --> 00:25:28,689
And now you've upset Edward.

437
00:25:28,827 --> 00:25:30,159
- (pops)
- (groans)

438
00:25:30,696 --> 00:25:31,857
As you see,

439
00:25:32,164 --> 00:25:33,757
more misfires.

440
00:25:33,899 --> 00:25:36,698
- Sir, if we don't
give better quality...
- Shut up.

441
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:38,202
Sir?

442
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:42,064
- Sir?
- Shh, shut up!

443
00:25:42,241 --> 00:25:43,241
Shut up.

444
00:25:44,243 --> 00:25:45,541
Do you hear that?

445
00:25:46,278 --> 00:25:47,712
(exhales)

446
00:25:47,946 --> 00:25:50,916
You said yourself, Penguin
has locked himself in City Hall

447
00:25:51,050 --> 00:25:52,916
- with a small army.
- I know that.

448
00:25:53,052 --> 00:25:55,021
- And I know you miss Butch.
- Do you?

449
00:25:55,154 --> 00:25:57,089
Because he only
did it to hurt me.

450
00:25:58,624 --> 00:26:00,115
That's why I have
to make it right.

451
00:26:00,259 --> 00:26:02,751
And how are you gonna
do that and not get killed?

452
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:07,097
I need you, too.

453
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:10,231
(helicopter whirring
faintly in distance)

454
00:26:10,569 --> 00:26:11,935
(whirring grows closer)

455
00:26:12,771 --> 00:26:14,239
Tabby, you hear me?

456
00:26:15,174 --> 00:26:16,665
Is that a chopper?

457
00:26:26,151 --> 00:26:27,175
There it is.

458
00:26:30,222 --> 00:26:31,588
This is Bruce Wayne.

459
00:26:31,723 --> 00:26:33,749
I'm at the GCPD. We can see you.

460
00:26:34,726 --> 00:26:36,326
PILOT (over radio):
<i>Copy that, Mr. Wayne.</i>

461
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:38,154
<i>We'll meet you at
the rendezvous point.</i>

462
00:26:49,007 --> 00:26:50,236
PILOT: <i>Mayday! Mayday!</i>

463
00:26:50,375 --> 00:26:51,855
<i>We've been hit!
We're going down hard.</i>

464
00:26:51,944 --> 00:26:53,955
- Harvey, the chopper went down.
- PILOT: <i>Mayday! Mayday!</i>

465
00:26:53,979 --> 00:26:55,259
GORDON: Get a team together now.

466
00:26:55,380 --> 00:26:57,849
PILOT: <i>Brace for
impact. We're going down.</i>

467
00:26:57,983 --> 00:26:59,212
Oh, my God.

468
00:27:05,357 --> 00:27:07,826
Chopper went down
in Lo Boyz territory.

469
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:09,952
I expect we'll have to
fight our way in and out.

470
00:27:10,095 --> 00:27:11,188
I know it's a lot to ask,

471
00:27:11,330 --> 00:27:12,958
but without those
supplies, we're done.

472
00:27:13,098 --> 00:27:15,009
Can we get some more ammo?
We're running dry down here.

473
00:27:15,033 --> 00:27:16,899
Be happy you got
what you got, and get in.

474
00:27:17,035 --> 00:27:19,004
GORDON: Alfred, I
expected to see Bruce here,

475
00:27:19,138 --> 00:27:21,282
- wanting to come along.
- Well, you'd think,
wouldn't you?

476
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:22,934
I mean, his chopper, his pilots.

477
00:27:23,375 --> 00:27:24,819
Maybe he thought
you wouldn't allow it.

478
00:27:24,843 --> 00:27:26,368
(engines starting)

479
00:27:26,712 --> 00:27:28,738
Just keep an eye on
things while I'm gone.

480
00:27:30,082 --> 00:27:31,345
(sirens whooping)

481
00:27:38,357 --> 00:27:40,849
(whirring, crackling)

482
00:27:40,993 --> 00:27:42,962
(indistinct chatter)

483
00:27:47,299 --> 00:27:49,063
(tires squealing)

484
00:27:56,942 --> 00:27:58,740
(car doors open)

485
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:02,680
Hello.

486
00:28:03,916 --> 00:28:07,045
The Lo Boyz, is it?

487
00:28:07,186 --> 00:28:08,186
(chuckles)

488
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:10,151
I suspect you know who I am.

489
00:28:10,889 --> 00:28:12,323
This ain't your turf, bird man.

490
00:28:12,724 --> 00:28:13,953
OSWALD: Be that as it may,

491
00:28:14,092 --> 00:28:16,152
I'm here to claim that.

492
00:28:18,764 --> 00:28:19,959
Like hell.

493
00:28:21,300 --> 00:28:22,427
(sighs)

494
00:28:25,771 --> 00:28:27,171
(men shouting, grunting)

495
00:28:29,441 --> 00:28:31,034
Get it in the truck.

496
00:28:31,977 --> 00:28:33,775
(tires squeal, siren whoops)

497
00:28:39,751 --> 00:28:40,912
Oswald!

498
00:28:41,353 --> 00:28:42,480
Jim.

499
00:28:43,188 --> 00:28:45,350
I thought you might show up.

500
00:28:46,291 --> 00:28:49,056
It is so good to
see you, old friend.

501
00:28:49,962 --> 00:28:52,431
How are you faring in
these troubled times?

502
00:28:53,131 --> 00:28:55,191
Tell your men to step
away from the chopper.

503
00:28:55,367 --> 00:28:58,360
Sorry. Mouths to feed.

504
00:28:59,304 --> 00:29:01,364
And you know all
about that, don't you?

505
00:29:02,074 --> 00:29:03,133
I hear you are up

506
00:29:03,275 --> 00:29:05,437
to your ears in refugees.

507
00:29:05,777 --> 00:29:08,076
We're protecting
children, families.

508
00:29:08,213 --> 00:29:09,476
We need those supplies.

509
00:29:10,148 --> 00:29:12,049
You shouldn't have
shot it down, Oswald.

510
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:14,913
You think I did this? (laughs)

511
00:29:15,053 --> 00:29:16,351
No, no, no, no, no.

512
00:29:17,055 --> 00:29:19,456
That would mean that I
knew a chopper was coming,

513
00:29:19,791 --> 00:29:21,953
which I did not. I mean,
don't get me wrong,

514
00:29:22,094 --> 00:29:23,294
we're still taking everything,

515
00:29:23,362 --> 00:29:25,922
but I did not fire the shot.

516
00:29:26,064 --> 00:29:27,157
It was an RPG.

517
00:29:27,299 --> 00:29:29,063
Who else has that
kind of firepower?

518
00:29:30,068 --> 00:29:31,161
Fair point.

519
00:29:32,004 --> 00:29:33,472
But if it was me,

520
00:29:34,172 --> 00:29:35,765
wouldn't I just admit it?

521
00:29:36,408 --> 00:29:38,070
(laughing): I mean,

522
00:29:38,210 --> 00:29:40,304
it's not like I'm
going to be arrested.

523
00:29:42,214 --> 00:29:43,443
Then who was it?

524
00:29:43,782 --> 00:29:44,841
No idea.

525
00:29:45,083 --> 00:29:47,143
Now, nice as it was catching up,

526
00:29:47,286 --> 00:29:49,050
it's time you skedaddle.

527
00:29:49,388 --> 00:29:50,913
While you can.

528
00:29:51,957 --> 00:29:54,051
We are, uh, kind of
outgunned here, partner.

529
00:29:54,192 --> 00:29:55,216
OSWALD: Listen to Harvey.

530
00:29:56,161 --> 00:29:57,857
After all we have been through,

531
00:29:57,996 --> 00:30:00,090
do not make me kill you.

532
00:30:01,133 --> 00:30:02,396
Not like this.

533
00:30:08,940 --> 00:30:11,466
(whooshing) (men groaning)

534
00:30:22,154 --> 00:30:24,419
(grunting and groaning)

535
00:30:28,427 --> 00:30:29,918
(gasping)

536
00:30:30,062 --> 00:30:32,190
- You should've stayed home.
- Listen to me.

537
00:30:33,265 --> 00:30:35,325
I know you're upset about Butch.

538
00:30:35,467 --> 00:30:36,491
(grunts)

539
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:37,945
He thought you were his friend!

540
00:30:37,969 --> 00:30:39,835
- I was his friend!
- Liar!

541
00:30:40,172 --> 00:30:42,198
You put a knife in
my mother's back.

542
00:30:42,341 --> 00:30:44,901
His blood is on your hands!

543
00:30:45,277 --> 00:30:48,543
You really think that I expected
to come here and walk away?

544
00:30:51,616 --> 00:30:52,927
Jim, are you just
going to let her

545
00:30:52,951 --> 00:30:54,544
kill me like this in cold blood?

546
00:30:55,287 --> 00:30:57,085
Jim, listen to me. You
are not the only one

547
00:30:57,222 --> 00:30:58,422
keeping Gotham from the abyss.

548
00:30:58,457 --> 00:31:00,153
I am! I provide stability!

549
00:31:00,292 --> 00:31:02,523
(gasps, pants)

550
00:31:04,596 --> 00:31:06,292
I may have pulled the trigger,

551
00:31:06,965 --> 00:31:09,093
but you killed Butch.

552
00:31:11,937 --> 00:31:13,496
Shut up and die.

553
00:31:14,606 --> 00:31:17,007
(pops, crackles)

554
00:31:20,379 --> 00:31:22,143
(laughing)

555
00:31:25,350 --> 00:31:26,545
(grunting)

556
00:31:27,219 --> 00:31:29,188
Now, if that was
one of my bullets,

557
00:31:29,321 --> 00:31:32,655
I will certainly be having
a word with my foreman.

558
00:31:33,225 --> 00:31:35,023
Unacceptable!

559
00:31:36,361 --> 00:31:38,887
Say hello to Butch.

560
00:31:39,030 --> 00:31:40,328
(strained grunting)

561
00:31:45,103 --> 00:31:48,039
BARBARA: <i>No...!</i>

562
00:31:50,675 --> 00:31:52,644
♪♪

563
00:32:05,257 --> 00:32:07,226
♪♪

564
00:32:13,498 --> 00:32:15,023
(whispering): Barbara...

565
00:32:15,167 --> 00:32:16,328
don't...

566
00:32:21,206 --> 00:32:22,697
(screaming)

567
00:32:28,580 --> 00:32:30,549
- (Barbara screaming)
- (gunshots)

568
00:32:48,567 --> 00:32:49,660
- I'm out.
- Me, too.

569
00:32:50,001 --> 00:32:51,001
OSWALD: Uh-oh, Jim!

570
00:32:51,036 --> 00:32:53,198
Sounding a little
quiet over there!

571
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:57,133
What the hell do we do now?

572
00:32:58,310 --> 00:33:00,040
(gunfire continues in distance)

573
00:33:04,149 --> 00:33:05,549
(grunting and groaning)

574
00:33:11,656 --> 00:33:13,625
(gunfire continues in distance)

575
00:33:21,466 --> 00:33:23,162
(screaming)

576
00:33:24,402 --> 00:33:25,529
(yells in pain)

577
00:33:28,139 --> 00:33:30,438
I know, I shouldn't
be here. But look.

578
00:33:30,675 --> 00:33:33,144
Penguin had a truck
out back. I took these.

579
00:33:33,545 --> 00:33:34,545
And there's more.

580
00:33:34,713 --> 00:33:36,181
I could kiss you, kid.

581
00:33:36,314 --> 00:33:38,442
OSWALD: For the
record, this is not

582
00:33:38,550 --> 00:33:40,041
how I wanted things to go.

583
00:33:40,185 --> 00:33:41,278
You son of a bitch.

584
00:33:42,187 --> 00:33:44,019
I will rip out your heart!

585
00:33:44,155 --> 00:33:46,624
Quiet. Now, that is
exactly the kind of talk

586
00:33:46,758 --> 00:33:48,317
that's gonna force my hand.

587
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:51,696
But for old time's sake,
I will give you a chance.

588
00:33:52,764 --> 00:33:54,596
Can we move past this?

589
00:33:55,534 --> 00:33:58,766
Say the whole
Tabitha-Butch chapter is over?

590
00:34:00,305 --> 00:34:03,332
I am gonna feed your guts

591
00:34:03,608 --> 00:34:05,076
to the rats,

592
00:34:05,343 --> 00:34:07,403
you beaky-nosed freak!

593
00:34:09,347 --> 00:34:10,576
So, no.

594
00:34:13,351 --> 00:34:14,819
What's the plan, boss?

595
00:34:16,488 --> 00:34:17,615
Cover me.

596
00:34:18,423 --> 00:34:19,652
GORDON: Oswald!

597
00:34:20,292 --> 00:34:21,590
I want to make a deal.

598
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:24,420
(chuckling): A deal, Jim?

599
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:28,624
We split whatever's
in the chopper 50-50...

600
00:34:30,335 --> 00:34:31,803
and you let Barbara go.

601
00:34:33,104 --> 00:34:34,104
No.

602
00:34:34,573 --> 00:34:37,270
He does not get to
limp out of here alive!

603
00:34:37,409 --> 00:34:38,138
(grunts)

604
00:34:38,276 --> 00:34:39,471
Shh!

605
00:34:41,212 --> 00:34:42,805
I got a deal for you, Jim.

606
00:34:43,348 --> 00:34:47,513
She dies, I take everything,
and you go home and reflect

607
00:34:47,652 --> 00:34:49,450
long and hard

608
00:34:49,588 --> 00:34:51,250
on my generosity.

609
00:34:51,389 --> 00:34:52,789
And if I say no?

610
00:34:53,725 --> 00:34:55,489
What happens when
the government finds out

611
00:34:55,627 --> 00:34:58,290
you murdered the only
cops left in Gotham?

612
00:35:00,165 --> 00:35:01,531
(laughing): Nothing.

613
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:04,364
Jim, as far as I can tell,

614
00:35:04,502 --> 00:35:07,666
you have nothing to offer,
and you're out of ammo.

615
00:35:10,842 --> 00:35:12,811
(shrieking)

616
00:35:14,212 --> 00:35:15,305
Not anymore.

617
00:35:17,716 --> 00:35:19,396
Truth is, I was never
gonna make that deal.

618
00:35:19,484 --> 00:35:21,544
I need all those
supplies. Load up!

619
00:35:22,821 --> 00:35:24,187
(screams)

620
00:35:32,664 --> 00:35:34,860
(dogs barking)

621
00:35:35,200 --> 00:35:36,862
MAN: <i>We got it.
Here we go, people.</i>

622
00:35:37,202 --> 00:35:39,603
<i>- Heads up.</i>
- WOMAN: <i>Finally, here we are.</i>

623
00:35:41,239 --> 00:35:43,117
BULLOCK: You think
Penguin's gonna pull through?

624
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:44,575
Cockroaches are hard to kill.

625
00:35:44,709 --> 00:35:46,487
But at least he'll be out
of commission for a while.

626
00:35:46,511 --> 00:35:47,591
You had him dead to rights.

627
00:35:47,646 --> 00:35:49,006
You could've put
him down for good.

628
00:35:49,180 --> 00:35:51,149
Yeah, shot a man
without warning.

629
00:35:51,282 --> 00:35:52,893
Three months ago, I
would've lost my badge for that.

630
00:35:52,917 --> 00:35:55,250
Three months ago, we
weren't fighting for our survival.

631
00:35:55,387 --> 00:35:56,753
You think it didn't
cross my mind?

632
00:35:57,222 --> 00:35:58,662
I know what we're
up against, Harvey.

633
00:35:59,391 --> 00:36:00,391
No one is coming to help.

634
00:36:00,525 --> 00:36:01,869
Then why didn't
you do us all a favor

635
00:36:01,893 --> 00:36:03,885
and put that murdering
son of a bitch in a hole?

636
00:36:04,729 --> 00:36:06,698
You want rules for
this game? I'll tell you.

637
00:36:06,831 --> 00:36:09,164
I'll make it simple,
okay? You win or you die.

638
00:36:09,300 --> 00:36:10,768
Next time, shoot to kill.

639
00:36:10,902 --> 00:36:13,872
♪♪

640
00:36:14,239 --> 00:36:15,239
Everything all right?

641
00:36:15,340 --> 00:36:16,364
No, but we're alive,

642
00:36:16,508 --> 00:36:17,908
so that's something. What's up?

643
00:36:18,243 --> 00:36:19,754
The-the medicine's just
been taken to the clinic.

644
00:36:19,778 --> 00:36:21,440
- I need to check on Selina.
- Yeah, sure.

645
00:36:21,579 --> 00:36:22,579
I'll get you a ride.

646
00:36:22,614 --> 00:36:24,810
- Hey! Let me know how she is.
- All right.

647
00:36:25,583 --> 00:36:26,778
And, Bruce?

648
00:36:29,354 --> 00:36:31,414
Next time you want
to help, just ask.

649
00:36:31,756 --> 00:36:33,349
You've earned a place here.

650
00:36:39,397 --> 00:36:41,366
♪♪

651
00:36:57,482 --> 00:36:58,973
WOMAN (over radio):
<i>Captain Gordon?</i>

652
00:36:59,317 --> 00:37:02,287
<i>Hello? Captain Gordon, come in.</i>

653
00:37:02,420 --> 00:37:04,412
(radio static warbling
and crackling)

654
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:09,660
<i>Captain Gordon, do you read me?</i>

655
00:37:11,496 --> 00:37:13,829
<i>Hello? Come in.</i>

656
00:37:14,265 --> 00:37:16,393
This is James Gordon.
Who am I speaking to?

657
00:37:17,268 --> 00:37:18,827
<i>A friend who wants you to know</i>

658
00:37:18,970 --> 00:37:20,563
<i>you have allies
across the river.</i>

659
00:37:20,972 --> 00:37:22,600
<i>We will find a way to help you.</i>

660
00:37:22,741 --> 00:37:23,741
And who are you?

661
00:37:23,908 --> 00:37:26,639
(radio crackling)

662
00:37:33,351 --> 00:37:36,287
♪♪

663
00:37:54,372 --> 00:37:56,841
(birds cawing, dogs barking)

664
00:37:56,975 --> 00:38:00,275
(muttering, humming)

665
00:38:02,514 --> 00:38:03,573
(grunts)

666
00:38:03,715 --> 00:38:05,377
(cat meowing nearby)

667
00:38:05,517 --> 00:38:06,517
(gasps)

668
00:38:07,519 --> 00:38:09,818
- Get out of here!
- (gasps, whimpers)

669
00:38:13,625 --> 00:38:14,649
Really?

670
00:38:15,527 --> 00:38:16,551
A dumpster?

671
00:38:18,630 --> 00:38:19,825
(panting)

672
00:38:24,702 --> 00:38:25,863
(sighs): Okay.

673
00:38:31,309 --> 00:38:32,368
(shouts)

674
00:38:32,510 --> 00:38:35,070
What are you doing to me?!

675
00:38:35,547 --> 00:38:37,311
Show yourself!

676
00:38:39,050 --> 00:38:41,315
What is happening to me?

677
00:38:41,653 --> 00:38:43,622
♪♪

678
00:39:19,958 --> 00:39:21,654
I promise...

679
00:39:24,429 --> 00:39:26,625
if it's the last thing I do...

680
00:39:28,900 --> 00:39:31,426
I will kill him!

681
00:39:31,569 --> 00:39:33,834
(Oswald screaming)

682
00:39:34,005 --> 00:39:35,871
Aah! My leg!

683
00:39:36,441 --> 00:39:39,741
He shot my leg!
I just fixed this!

684
00:39:39,878 --> 00:39:42,438
Mr. Cobblepot, if
you could hold still, I...

685
00:39:42,580 --> 00:39:43,445
Put out the word.

686
00:39:43,581 --> 00:39:47,416
100,000 rounds of ammunition
to whoever kills Jim Gordon.

687
00:39:47,785 --> 00:39:49,651
I want his head.

688
00:39:49,787 --> 00:39:51,449
(screaming)

689
00:39:56,961 --> 00:39:58,793
(wheels squeaking)

690
00:40:15,780 --> 00:40:17,942
(door creaks shut)

691
00:40:20,652 --> 00:40:21,984
(gasps, grunts)

692
00:40:22,687 --> 00:40:23,687
(grunts)

693
00:40:25,023 --> 00:40:26,992
(Selina screaming, sobbing)

694
00:40:28,493 --> 00:40:29,893
No!

695
00:40:30,528 --> 00:40:31,188
No!

696
00:40:31,529 --> 00:40:32,690
- Selina.
- DOCTOR: Help!

697
00:40:32,830 --> 00:40:34,628
Let me go!

698
00:40:34,766 --> 00:40:36,428
- Selina. Selina.
- Let me go!

699
00:40:36,567 --> 00:40:37,796
Selina...

700
00:40:37,936 --> 00:40:39,529
(crying): You can't
do this. Please.

701
00:40:39,671 --> 00:40:41,606
(crying continues)

702
00:40:41,739 --> 00:40:43,105
I have no reason to...

703
00:40:43,441 --> 00:40:44,441
I can't...

704
00:40:44,742 --> 00:40:46,506
(gasping)

705
00:40:54,786 --> 00:40:56,948
You should've just let me do it.

706
00:40:59,857 --> 00:41:00,857
Let her do what?

707
00:41:00,992 --> 00:41:02,051
What happened?

708
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:04,695
She was trying to kill herself.

709
00:41:06,030 --> 00:41:08,192
I'll get restraints
for when she wakes.

710
00:41:11,135 --> 00:41:13,104
♪♪

711
00:41:15,073 --> 00:41:16,803
(door creaks open)

712
00:41:18,176 --> 00:41:20,736
I told you, you
want to cure her,

713
00:41:21,045 --> 00:41:22,741
you have to go to the witch.

714
00:41:25,717 --> 00:41:27,686
And where do I find this witch?

715
00:41:28,686 --> 00:41:30,621
(birds squawking)

716
00:41:33,057 --> 00:41:34,616
- Thank you so much.
- No problem.

717
00:41:34,759 --> 00:41:35,759
Thank you very much.

718
00:41:35,793 --> 00:41:38,058
Saint Jim of Gotham. All right.

719
00:41:40,064 --> 00:41:42,966
Hey. Every new refugee who
comes in, I want questioned.

720
00:41:43,101 --> 00:41:44,899
I need information
on Jeremiah Valeska.

721
00:41:45,036 --> 00:41:46,146
I haven't heard
that clown's name

722
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:47,798
in three months. Why now?

723
00:41:48,673 --> 00:41:49,868
Just call it a hunch.

724
00:41:50,508 --> 00:41:52,875
Well, rather than a week
of food, we've got six weeks.

725
00:41:53,011 --> 00:41:54,104
It's not a lot.

726
00:41:54,245 --> 00:41:55,838
Yeah, but it's
better than we were.

727
00:41:56,014 --> 00:41:57,107
Don't give up hope.

728
00:41:57,248 --> 00:41:58,580
MAN: <i>Captain Gordon!</i>

729
00:41:58,750 --> 00:41:59,877
Captain Gordon!

730
00:42:02,186 --> 00:42:03,552
What's going on?

731
00:42:04,655 --> 00:42:05,655
MAN: I was on duty

732
00:42:05,723 --> 00:42:06,934
at the Thompson
Street barricade.

733
00:42:06,958 --> 00:42:08,790
(panting): He just appeared.

734
00:42:08,926 --> 00:42:10,656
He said he needed to see you.

735
00:42:11,062 --> 00:42:12,189
What happened, son?

736
00:42:12,830 --> 00:42:13,923
Where'd you come from?

737
00:42:15,666 --> 00:42:17,026
(whispers): Past
the train station.

738
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:18,679
BULLOCK: That's on
the other side of town.

739
00:42:18,703 --> 00:42:19,813
This kid must've made it through

740
00:42:19,837 --> 00:42:21,601
half a dozen
sectors to get here.

741
00:42:21,973 --> 00:42:23,703
My brothers and sisters.

742
00:42:25,109 --> 00:42:26,133
They're killing us.

743
00:42:26,544 --> 00:42:27,544
Who is?

744
00:42:28,279 --> 00:42:30,077
You have to help us.

745
00:42:30,815 --> 00:42:31,815
Whoa, whoa.

746
00:42:32,216 --> 00:42:33,684
Get him to the clinic.

747
00:42:33,818 --> 00:42:35,787
(gasps, coughs)

748
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:52,871
I know you're all asking,
why are we still here

749
00:42:53,004 --> 00:42:55,064
when our own
government won't help us?

750
00:42:56,107 --> 00:42:57,575
It's simple.

751
00:43:00,244 --> 00:43:02,645
We're supposed to be
giving these people hope.

752
00:43:04,749 --> 00:43:07,583
Hope that if they're in
danger, someone will come.

753
00:43:09,887 --> 00:43:11,651
We will come.

754
00:43:14,058 --> 00:43:15,287
Suit up!
